.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt DSH.DSM 1
.Os "dsh.dsm (@VERSION@)"
.Sh NAME
.Nm dsh.dsm
.Nd distributed shell (IBM DSM dialect)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | Fl V | Fl q
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl n Ar node_list
.Op Fl N Ar nodegroups
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl f Ar fanout
.Op Fl t Ar timeout
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl l Ar user
.Op Fl o Dq Ar node_options
.Op Fl r Ar node_remote_shell
.Op Fl S Ar csh|ksh
.Op Fl X Op Ar env_list
.Op command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs a command in parallel across a set of node targets, tagging each line of
output with the name of the node it came from.  It is the
.Em DSM
dialect of
.Xr dsh 1 ,
following the command grammar of the IBM AIX Distributed Systems Management
.Nm dsh
utility rather than the PSSP grammar of
.Xr dsh.pssp 1 .
Both dialects share one engine and are coinstallable; the plain
.Nm dsh
name resolves to whichever dialect the build selected as the default.
.Pp
The target list is the union of the nodes named with
.Fl n ,
the members of the node groups named with
.Fl N ,
and, with
.Fl a ,
every node in every group file found on
.Ev DSH_NODEGROUP_PATH .
If no targets are given on the command line, the file named by
.Ev DSH_NODE_LIST
is read instead (one target per line; blank lines and lines beginning with
.Ql #
are ignored).
.Pp
A target token may contain a single bracketed numeric range or list, for
example
.Ic node[1-4,7] ,
which expands to
.Ic node1 node2 node3 node4 node7 .
The low bound sets the zero-pad width, so
.Ic n[08-10]
yields
.Ic n08 n09 n10 .
.Pp
The remote shell is
.Xr ssh 1
or
.Xr rsh 1
as chosen by
.Fl r
or
.Ev DSH_NODE_RSH ;
options for it come from
.Fl o
or
.Ev DSH_NODE_OPTS .
By default output is held per target and printed in a block once that target
finishes;
.Fl s
streams each target's output as it arrives instead.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n Ar node_list
A comma- or space-separated list of node targets, with optional bracket
ranges.  May be given more than once; the lists are unioned.
.It Fl N Ar nodegroups
A comma-separated list of node group names.  Each is looked up as a file of
the same name in a directory on
.Ev DSH_NODEGROUP_PATH ;
its members are added to the target list.
.It Fl a
Add every node in every group file found on
.Ev DSH_NODEGROUP_PATH .
.It Fl f Ar fanout
Maximum number of remote shell processes to run concurrently.  A value of 1
runs serially.  The default is 64, capped to what the open-file limit allows.
.It Fl t Ar timeout
Seconds to wait for output from a remote target.  If none arrives within the
timeout, an error is reported for that target.  The default is to wait
indefinitely.
.It Fl s
Streaming mode: return output as it becomes available from each target rather
than holding and ordering it per target.  Output is then unsorted.
.It Fl v
Verify each target with a ping before running; a target that does not respond
is dropped.
.It Fl l Ar user
Run the remote command as
.Ar user
rather than the local user name.
.It Fl o Dq Ar node_options
Options to pass to the remote shell command.  Quote them so they are not
parsed as
.Nm
options.
.It Fl r Ar node_remote_shell
The remote shell command used to reach node targets, overriding
.Ev DSH_NODE_RSH .
.It Fl S Ar csh|ksh
Remote shell syntax used when exporting
.Ev DSH_PATH
to the target.  The default is
.Ic ksh .
.It Fl X Op Ar env_list
Ignore the
.Ev DSH_*
environment variables.  With an attached comma-separated
.Ar env_list
( Fl X Ns Ar list ),
only the named variables are kept; with no argument, all are ignored.
.It Fl q
Display the resolved configuration (remote shell, fanout, timeout, syntax,
group path, node-list source) and exit.
.It Fl V
Display version information and exit.
.It Fl h
Display usage information and exit.
.It Op Ar command
The command to run on each target.  With no command,
.Nm
enters interactive mode.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev DSH_NODE_LIST
A file of node targets, one per line, used when no targets are named on the
command line.  This replaced PSSP's
.Ev WCOLL .
.It Ev DSH_NODEGROUP_PATH
A colon-separated list of directories holding node group files, searched by
.Fl N
and
.Fl a .
.It Ev DSH_NODE_RSH
The remote shell command for node targets.  Overridden by
.Fl r .
.It Ev DSH_NODE_OPTS
Options for the remote shell command.  Overridden by
.Fl o .
.It Ev DSH_FANOUT
The default fanout.  Overridden by
.Fl f .
.It Ev DSH_TIMEOUT
The default timeout in seconds.  Overridden by
.Fl t .
.It Ev DSH_SYNTAX
The default remote syntax, csh or ksh.  Overridden by
.Fl S .
.It Ev DSH_PATH
A
.Ev PATH
to set on the target before running the command.  If unset or empty, no
.Ev PATH
is set.
.It Ev DSH_DEBUG
If set, emit debugging information.
.El
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
.Nm
follows the node-side grammar of the IBM AIX DSM
.Nm dsh
command.  Device targets
.Pq Fl d , Fl D , Fl O , Fl A
and the IBM DSM/CSM/NIM reporting and monitoring infrastructure are not
implemented; they have no backend on a generic host.  The context selectors
.Fl C
and
.Fl D
are reserved for pluggable context modules, not yet available.  Several
defined flags
.Pq Fl z , Fl Q , Fl F , Fl m , Fl T , Fl i , Fl c , Fl L , --log
and script copy
.Pq Fl e , Fl E
are planned and are reported as not implemented rather than silently ignored.
